    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "(function () {\n  'use strict';\n\n  const form = document.getElementById('settings-form');\n  const workInput = document.getElementById('work-seconds');\n  const restInput = document.getElementById('rest-seconds');\n  const roundsInput = document.getElementById('rounds');\n  const startBtn = document.getElementById('start-btn');\n  const phaseEl = document.getElementById('phase');\n  const timeEl = document.getElementById('time');\n  const roundEl = document.getElementById('round');\n  const completionEl = document.getElementById('completion-message');\n  const errorEl = document.getElementById('error-message');\n\n  let timerId = null;\n  let state = null;\n\n  function showError(msg) {\n    errorEl.textContent = msg;\n    errorEl.hidden = false;\n  }\n\n  function clearError() {\n    errorEl.hidden = true;\n    errorEl.textContent = '';\n  }\n\n  function stopTimer() {\n    if (timerId !== null) {\n      clearInterval(timerId);\n      timerId = null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function setControlsDisabled(disabled) {\n    workInput.disabled = disabled;\n    restInput.disabled = disabled;\n    roundsInput.disabled = disabled;\n    startBtn.disabled = disabled;\n    startBtn.textContent = disabled ? 'Running...' : 'Start';\n  }\n\n  function updateDisplay() {\n    if (!state) return;\n    phaseEl.textContent = state.phase === 'work' ? 'Work' : state.phase === 'rest' ? 'Rest' : 'Ready';\n    timeEl.textContent = String(state.remaining);\n    roundEl.textContent = 'Round ' + state.round + ' / ' + state.totalRounds;\n  }\n\n  function speak(text) {\n    if ('speechSynthesis' in window) {\n      try {\n        const utterance = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(text);\n        utterance.rate = 1;\n        utterance.pitch = 1;\n        window.speechSynthesis.speak(utterance);\n      } catch (e) {\n        // Speech not available; ignore.\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function finishWorkout() {\n    stopTimer();\n    state.phase = 'done';\n    phaseEl.textContent = 'Done';\n    timeEl.textContent = '0';\n    completionEl.hidden = false;\n    setControlsDisabled(false);\n    speak('Workout complete');\n    state = null;\n  }\n\n  function tick() {\n    if (!state) return;\n    state.remaining -= 1;\n    if (state.remaining > 0) {\n      updateDisplay();\n      return;\n    }\n    // Phase ended\n    if (state.phase === 'work') {\n      if (state.round >= state.totalRounds) {\n        finishWorkout();\n        return;\n      }\n      state.phase = 'rest';\n      state.remaining = state.restSeconds;\n      updateDisplay();\n    } else if (state.phase === 'rest') {\n      state.round += 1;\n      state.phase = 'work';\n      state.remaining = state.workSeconds;\n      updateDisplay();\n    }\n  }\n\n  function startWorkout(workSeconds, restSeconds, totalRounds) {\n    stopTimer();\n    clearError();\n    completionEl.hidden = true;\n    state = {\n      phase: 'work',\n      remaining: workSeconds,\n      round: 1,\n      totalRounds: totalRounds,\n      workSeconds: workSeconds,\n      restSeconds: restSeconds\n    };\n    updateDisplay();\n    setControlsDisabled(true);\n    timerId = setInterval(tick, 1000);\n  }\n\n  function parsePositiveInt(value, name, max) {\n    const num = Number(value);\n    if (!Number.isInteger(num) || num < 1 || num > max) {\n      throw new Error(name + ' must be a whole number between 1 and ' + max + '.');\n    }\n    return num;\n  }\n\n  form.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    clearError();\n    let workSeconds, restSeconds, totalRounds;\n    try {\n      workSeconds = parsePositiveInt(workInput.value, 'Work seconds', 999);\n      restSeconds = parsePositiveInt(restInput.value, 'Rest seconds', 999);\n      totalRounds = parsePositiveInt(roundsInput.value, 'Rounds', 99);\n    } catch (err) {\n      showError(err.message);\n      return;\n    }\n    startWorkout(workSeconds, restSeconds, totalRounds);\n  });\n\n  // Allow starting with Enter key inside inputs (form submit handles it).\n  // No additional key handling needed.\n})();",
      "description": "Unchanged timer logic."
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Interval Trainer\n\nA simple offline interval trainer built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Set work seconds, rest seconds, and rounds, then start a countdown that alternates between work and rest phases. At the end, it displays and speaks \"Workout complete\".\n\n## Features\n\n- Set work duration, rest duration, and number of rounds.\n- Countdown timer with clear phase (Work/Rest) and round indicators.\n- Keyboard-accessible labeled inputs and a Start button.\n- Visual feedback for hover, focus, and pressed states.\n- Responsive layout down to 360px width.\n- Uses the SpeechSynthesis API to announce \"Workout complete\" when supported.\n- No external dependencies, network requests, or assets.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter your desired work seconds, rest seconds, and rounds.\n3. Click **Start** (or press Enter while focused on an input).\n4. The timer will count down work, then rest, repeating for each round.\n5. When all rounds are finished, a completion message appears and is spoken.\n\n## Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- **Tab** / **Shift+Tab**: Move focus between controls.\n- **Enter**: Submit the form (start the workout) when focused on an input or the Start button.\n- **Space**: Activate the Start button when focused.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` – Page structure and controls.\n- `style.css` – Theming and responsive layout.\n- `script.js` – Timer logic, validation, and speech output.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Speech output depends on browser support for the SpeechSynthesis API. If unavailable, the visual completion message still appears.\n- Timer accuracy may vary slightly due to browser scheduling; it is suitable for casual interval training.\n- Input values are validated to be whole numbers within reasonable limits (work/rest 1–999, rounds 1–99).",
      "description": "Unchanged documentation."
    }
  ]
